  },
  {
    topic: "YouTube and ads",
    rule: "YouTube lets a creator earn from ads if they are 18 or have a legal guardian over 18 who handles the AdSense payments. Memberships and Super Chat need the creator to be 18. AdSense itself accepts only applicants aged 18 or more, and a parent can apply with their own account.",
    means: "Start the channel for practice and proof. Let a parent set up the payment side later.",
  },
  {
    topic: "Marketplaces and social apps",
    rule: "Instagram lists 13 as its minimum age. Fiverr's help centre is reported to require 18, with a parent-account route for ages 13 to 17. Upwork staff have said users must be 18. Check each platform's current terms yourself, because they change.",
    means: "Do not lie about your age to get an account. A banned account also bans your money and your reviews.",
  },
  {
    topic: "Paid work under 18",
    rule: "Child and adolescent labour law restricts employing under-14s and bars adolescents (14 to 18) from hazardous work. Your own small online service is different from being employed in a workshop or factory.",
    means: "Stay with clean, desk, online or teaching work. We did not read the Act's full text, so ask a lawyer if a customer offers you physical or machine work.",
  },
];

