    A simple way to test any idea: your price minus the cost of one sale gives the money left per sale. Multiply by the sales you honestly expect, then take away fixed costs. The <a href="/tools/student-business-idea-feasibility-calculator/">student business idea feasibility calculator</a> does this arithmetic with your own numbers. It does not know if customers will buy, so use it to see the risk, not to promise yourself a profit.
